n irises and dark pupils that lock the viewer\\u2019s gaze. - The nose is cleanly defined with a soft brown top and darker nostril area, anchored by a crisp philtrum line. - A white muzzle and chin tuft add high contrast, making the mouth area read clearly even at distance. - **Mane Composition:** - The mane radiates outward in layered, flame-like sections, each panel defined by sharp black edges and internal color steps. - The bottom of the mane resolves into a tapered, almost emblem-like point, making this design ideal for vertically oriented placements. Impact on Skin & Ideal Placements This lion head tattoo design is created to hold strong on the body over time. The bold outlines and clean separation between color values ensure it reads clearly from across the room while still rewarding close inspection with subtle detailing around the eyes and muzzle. On the **forearm (inner or outer)**, the elongated taper of the mane naturally follows the arm\\u2019s line, creating a powerful totem-like presence. The symmetrical, frontal gaze makes it perfect for a forearm piece that faces outward when the hand is relaxed, projecting confidence and authority. Placed on the **calf**, the design becomes a vertical shield: the rounded upper mane fills the widest part of the muscle while the pointed lower section flows toward the ankle. This placement benefits from the design\\u2019s strong contrast, maintaining visibility even on more muscular or curved surfaces. For a **sternum or center-chest** application, the lion becomes a true centerpiece. The symmetrical structure aligns with the body\\u2019s vertical axis, with the upper mane sitting across the pectorals and the lower mane pointing toward the solar plexus. The direct, unflinching gaze enhances the sense of inner strength and personal sovereignty. Collectors seeking a **back-of-arm, thigh, or upper-back** design will also find this piece highly adaptable, as its clean, isolated subject can be easily framed with additional elements, script, or ornamental motifs if desired. Professional-Grade Digital Asset Specs - High-resolution digital tattoo design suitable for printing and resizing - Clean, isolated subject on a plain background for easy integration - Stencil-ready structure with clear, readable linework for professional use - Ideal as tattoo flash, digital reference, or client preview artwork - Compatible with standard printing formats for thermal stencil machines - Crisp details preserved for both small and large-scale placements --- Bold neo-traditional lion head tattoo design with strong linework, stencil-ready structure, and high-res digital download. Perfect for forearm, calf, or chest. Shop now.\"}, \"url\": \"https://tattty.com/products/lion-majesty-illustration\", \"handle\": \"lion-majesty-illustration\", \"price_range\": {\"min\": {\"amount\": 99, \"currency\": \"USD\"}, \"max\": {\"amount\": 99, \"currency\": \"USD\"}}, \"list_price_range\": {\"min\": {\"amount\": 1000, \"currency\": \"USD\"}, \"max\": {\"amount\": 1000, \"currency\": \"USD\"}}, \"variants\": [{\"id\": \"gid://shopify/ProductVariant/42203243053131\", \"title\": \"Default Title\", \"description\": {\"html\": \"Roaring Presence for Powerful Ink This lion head tattoo design is built for collectors who want their ink to speak before they do. A bold, neo-traditional style treatment frames the king of beasts as a clean, isolated subject, perfect as a stencil-ready centerpiece on the body. Strong linework, sculpted shading, and commanding eye contact create a digital reference that translates seamlessly from tattoo flash sheet to finished skin. Whether you\\u2019re a professional artist or a serious client planning your next large piece, this design balances aggression, elegance, and clarity for maximum impact. Anatomy & Flow of the Design The lion\\u2019s face is presented in a strict frontal view, symmetrical and dead-center, emphasizing strength and balance. - **Linework:** - Heavy, confident outer contour